menu "BabyTalk engine memory (sram_pool)"
config SRAM_POOL_IN_PSRAM
    bool "Put the engines' shared 84.5 KB block in PSRAM"
    default n
    help
        The speech engines (MMRT's staging buffers, sanoTTS's arena) share one 84.5 KB block,
        by default in internal SRAM, where they run fastest. On a board short of internal RAM
        (a camera, a display, WiFi and TLS all want it) put it in PSRAM instead: everything
        works the same, a little slower (octal PSRAM) or noticeably slower (quad PSRAM).
        The block can then also be taken at any time, not only at boot.
endmenu
